e an object that's a stream (so `makeStream` is called)\n2. The stream's dictionary should have a \"Length\" that references another object (indirect reference)\n3. When that \"Length\" object is fetched, it should trigger reading more of the XRef table\n4. Reading more of the XRef table should cause the entries array to be reallocated (grown)\n5. After reallocation, the `entry` pointer saved at the top of `makeStream` is dangling\n6. When `entry->setFlag(XRefEntry::Parsing, false)` is called, it's a use-after-free\n\nLet me look at how the XRef entries are managed and how they can be resized.",
